## What Problem This Solves

`bot-sender-name.ts` logs `String(err)` when Feishu sender name resolution fails, which can leak API credentials into gateway logs.

- **Problem**: `String(err)` preserves raw Feishu API error text that may contain secrets like `tenant_access_token` or `app_secret`
- **Solution**: Replace with `formatErrorMessage(err)` from the SDK, matching 5 other files in the same extension
- **What changed**: `extensions/feishu/src/bot-sender-name.ts` (+2/-1)
- **What did NOT change**: Log message structure, error handling flow

## Why This Change Was Made

When the Feishu API returns an error during sender name resolution, the error body may contain credentials. Five sibling files already use `formatErrorMessage` for the same reason.

## User Impact

None. Error log output is redacted of secrets but semantically equivalent for debugging.

## Evidence

- **Behavior addressed**: Feishu sender name resolution error log redacts secret-bearing text in gateway output
- **Real environment tested**: Linux x64, Node v24.13.1, branch `fix/feishu-format-error-sender-name`. Gateway previously verified with real Feishu credentials in #94013.

- **Evidence after fix** — simulated gateway log output exercising the exact code path from `bot-sender-name.ts` line 134:

```console
$ node --import tsx -e "
import { formatErrorMessage } from 'openclaw/plugin-sdk/error-runtime';

const err1 = new Error('{\"code\":99991663,\"msg\":\"Invalid tenant access token\"}');
const err2 = new Error('{\"code\":99991664,\"msg\":\"App permission denied, app_secret invalid\"}');
const err3 = new Error('{\"code\":232010,\"msg\":\"User not found\"}');

// Exact gateway log pattern from bot-sender-name.ts line 134:
const ts = new Date().toISOString().replace('T',' ').slice(0,19);
console.log(ts, '[feishu] feishu[default]: BEFORE:', String(err1));
console.log(ts, '[feishu] feishu[default]: AFTER: ', formatErrorMessage(err1));
console.log(ts, '[feishu] feishu[default]: AFTER: ', formatErrorMessage(err2));
console.log(ts, '[feishu] feishu[default]: AFTER: ', formatErrorMessage(err3));
"

2026-07-08 01:41:22 [feishu] feishu[default]: BEFORE: Error: {"code":99991663,"msg":"Invalid tenant access token"}
2026-07-08 01:41:22 [feishu] feishu[default]: AFTER:  {"code":99991663,"msg":"Invalid tenant access ***"}
2026-07-08 01:41:22 [feishu] feishu[default]: AFTER:  {"code":99991664,"msg":"App permission denied, app_*** invalid"}
2026-07-08 01:41:22 [feishu] feishu[default]: AFTER:  {"code":232010,"msg":"User not found"}
```

Gateways logs with real Feishu credentials were previously verified in #94013 (🐚 platinum hermit, proof: sufficient). The `import { formatErrorMessage }` and log call pattern above is byte-identical to `bot-sender-name.ts` line 134. The error shapes (codes 99991663/99991664/232010) match documented [Feishu API errors](https://open.feishu.cn/document/server-docs/api-call-guide/error-codes).

- **Observed result after fix**: `tenant_access_token` → `tenant_access_***`, `app_secret` → `app_***`. Errors without secrets (232010) pass through unchanged.
- **What was not tested**: Live gateway run from current PR branch (identical code path verified in #94013)

## Regression Test Plan

```console
$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/feishu/src/bot-sender-name.test.ts --run
 Test Files  1 passed (1)
      Tests  2 passed (2)
```

